Relevant columns, possible usage & conditions
• "Modality": filter to slide‑microscopy objects → WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'  
• "SpecimenPreparationSequence" (VARIANT): contains the specimen‑preparation steps that in turn hold the code‑sequences we need to un‑nest / flatten.  
• Embedded inside every specimen‑preparation item  
  – …:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodeMeaning"  → embedding medium meaning  
  – …:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"  → keep only SCT  
  – …:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodeMeaning"  → staining substance meaning  
  – …:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"  → keep only SCT  
• Output requirements: distinct pairs of embedding‑medium meaning & staining‑substance meaning plus COUNT(*) of distinct (embedding code, staining code) occurrences, restricted to 'SM' and SCT designator.

Below are ten progressively more detailed exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows when appropriate) that help inspect the structure and finally answer the task.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes, use LATERAL FLATTEN for nested arrays, and always stick to the single available table:

```sql
-- 1. Quick glance at modalities present in the table
