The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'IDC': {'IDC_V17': ['DICOM_METADATA']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, possible usage & conditions
• "Modality": filter to slide‑microscopy objects → WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'  
• "SpecimenPreparationSequence" (VARIANT): contains the specimen‑preparation steps that in turn hold the code‑sequences we need to un‑nest / flatten.  
• Embedded inside every specimen‑preparation item  
  – …:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodeMeaning"  → embedding medium meaning  
  – …:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"  → keep only SCT  
  – …:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodeMeaning"  → staining substance meaning  
  – …:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[ ]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"  → keep only SCT  
• Output requirements: distinct pairs of embedding‑medium meaning & staining‑substance meaning plus COUNT(*) of distinct (embedding code, staining code) occurrences, restricted to 'SM' and SCT designator.

Below are ten progressively more detailed exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows when appropriate) that help inspect the structure and finally answer the task.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes, use LATERAL FLATTEN for nested arrays, and always stick to the single available table:

```sql
-- 1. Quick glance at modalities present in the table
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Count how many studies/instances use slide‑microscopy modality ('SM')
SELECT COUNT(*) AS sm_rows
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "Modality" = 'SM';
```

```sql
-- 3. Show one raw specimen‑preparation array to understand its JSON structure
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "SpecimenPreparationSequence"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'
  AND "SpecimenPreparationSequence" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Flatten the top‑level SpecimenPreparationSequence items (1 row per prep step)
SELECT t."SOPInstanceUID",
       f.value AS specimen_prep_item
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect the JSON keys inside one flattened specimen‑preparation item
SELECT DISTINCT
       OBJECT_KEYS(f.value) AS prep_item_keys
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Dig into EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence content (first element only)
SELECT
  f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING      AS embedding_code_meaning,
  f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING AS embedding_designator
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0] IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Dig into StainingSubstanceCodeSequence content (first element only)
SELECT
  f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING          AS staining_code_meaning,
  f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING AS staining_designator
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0] IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Make sure both embedding & staining code sequences exist and come from SCT
SELECT
  f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING   AS embedding_meaning,
  f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING    AS staining_meaning
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING = 'SCT'
  AND f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING  = 'SCT'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Retrieve distinct embedding/staining meaning pairs (SCT only), no counts yet
SELECT DISTINCT
       f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING   AS embedding_meaning,
       f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING    AS staining_meaning
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING = 'SCT'
  AND f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING  = 'SCT'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: unique pairs with occurrence count (distinct by codes), SCT only
SELECT
  f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING   AS embedding_meaning,
  f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeMeaning"::STRING    AS staining_meaning,
  COUNT(DISTINCT
        f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeValue"::STRING
        || '|' ||
        f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodeValue"::STRING
       ) AS pair_count
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE t."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND f.value:"EmbeddingMediaTypeCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING = 'SCT'
  AND f.value:"StainingSubstanceCodeSequence"[0]:"CodingSchemeDesignator"::STRING  = 'SCT'
GROUP BY
  embedding_meaning,
  staining_meaning
ORDER BY
  pair_count DESC,
  embedding_meaning,
  staining_meaning
LIMIT 20;
```

